Subject: Phase3 Quiescent Double Inventory Semantic Authority Fault

& [FaultIdentity] is exact
  + [fault_uuid] is 46ac61cb-4689-4c35-94dd-586d5a294bd5
  + [detected_after] is supplied digest reconciliation proof closure
  + [status] is contained_before_M2C

& [Conflict] is public machine meaning
  + existing shared ConsistencyClass exposes quiescent_double_inventory
  + TopologyReceipt 0.2 requires that value
  + scanner formation assigns it from two repeated inventories
  + current reconciliation authority states quiescence additionally requires lifecycle and writer accounting

& [WhyItMatters] is honesty and security
  + equal observations can miss transient change-and-restore
  + equal observations say nothing about a change after the second observation
  + supervisor process accounting does not by itself exclude external writers
  + a state-sounding label can be used as authority stronger than its proof lineage

& [Containment] is complete
  + no physical scanner, receipt issuer, persisted receipt, mutation consumer, or external consumer exists
  + M2C, M2D, receipt issuance, mutation, sealing, and every physical effect remain locked
  + no existing implementation has emitted the value as physical evidence

& [Repair] is selected but unsigned
  + preserve a revision source for explicit InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + select non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal as the weakest future repeated physical acquisition grade
  + rename TopologyReceipt.consistency to consistency_evidence
  + revise affected profiles and reject legacy serialized forms
  + run full SJS and replacement signature before code

& [HistoricalRecord] remains immutable
  + prior formation fault correctly rejected atomic snapshot meaning but its retained quiescent label is now superseded by more precise analysis
  + historical source, specifications, proofs, and manifests remain attributable to their original authority state
